A:Wales
H:From a facsimile c.1840: A Choice Collection of Fifty-One Welsh Airs adapted for The Harp, Piano-Forte, Harpsichord, Violin, or Flute by Edward Jones "Harper to His Late Majesty King George IV, when Prince of Wales".
N:I'm not quite sure how Mr Jones thought this was "adapted for  the
N:violin or flute".  Part A is in the treble clef; Part B is in the
N:bass clef and should be played an octave lower than written. BM.
